      "description": "Lecturer, Computing Sciences - Houston, Texas, United States Lecturer, Computing Sciences - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Lecturer, Computing Sciences 497317 Full-Time Computing Sciences Department : Computing Sciences Salary : Commensurate with Experience/Education Description : The Computer Science Program in the College of Science and Engineering at University of Houston–Clear Lake (UHCL) invites applications for a full-time Lecturer in Computer Science position, with an anticipated start date of August 2027. The program seeks an educator with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, student engagement, academic advising, and service. The Computer Science Program offers Bachelor of Science (B.S.) and Master of Science (M.S.) degrees in Computer Science. The B.S. degree is ABET-accredited and emphasizes a strong foundation in computing theory, software development, systems, and emerging technologies. The successful candidate will contribute to the instructional mission of the Computer Science Program through high-quality teaching, student mentoring, curriculum support, and service activities. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate Computer Science courses and, depending on qualifications and program needs, graduate-level courses. Areas of instruction may include, but are not limited to, computing theory, programming, algorithms, data structures, database systems, computer organization, software engineering, systems analysis and design, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, cloud computing, and related computing disciplines. The Lecturer will be expected to maintain currency in the computing profession, employ effective and innovative teaching practices, utilize instructional technologies, assess student learning outcomes, participate in curriculum development and continuous improvement efforts, support accreditation and assessment activities, collaborate with faculty colleagues, and contribute to student recruitment, retention, and success initiatives. The position also requires active engagement in departmental, college, university, and professional service activities consistent with the mission of a teaching-focused institution. Full consideration will be given to applications received by January 15, 2027. Duties: Teach undergraduate Computer Science courses and, when qualified, graduate Computer Science courses. Advise and mentor undergraduate students and support student success initiatives. Assist with curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation-related activities. Participate in service to the program, college, university, and professional community. Collaborate with faculty and staff to support academic excellence and program growth. Qualifications Required: Master’s degree in Computer Science or a closely related field Candidates must demonstrate a strong commitment to effective teaching and student success Preferred: Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field Qualifications to teach both undergraduate and graduate Computer Science courses Demonstrated teaching experience in areas such as algorithms, data structures, database systems, systems analysis and design, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, and related computing disciplines Required Attachments by Candidate: 1) Curriculum Vitae, 2) a Letter of Application that addresses the required and preferred qualifications, and highlights teaching philosophy and experience, 3) unofficial graduate transcripts Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be requested for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews, and a background check will be required. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) edc66156 Last Name (required) a728e197 Email (required) d815b8fb Cell number 270a10e6 244 results found No results found United States (+1) United Kingdom (+44) Australia (+61) Ireland (+353) Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) Côte d’Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Curaçao (+599) Cyprus (+357) Czechia (+420) Denmark (+45) Djibouti (+253) Dominica (+1) Dominican Republic (+1) Ecuador (+593) Egypt (+20) El Salvador (+503) Equatorial Guinea (+240) Eritrea (+291) Estonia (+372) Eswatini (+268) Ethiopia (+251) Falkland Islands (Islas Malvinas) (+500) Faroe Islands (+298) Fiji (+679) Finland (+358) France (+33) French Guiana (+594) French Polynesia (+689) Gabon (+241) Gambia (+220) Georgia (+995) Germany (+49) Ghana (+233) Gibraltar (+350) Greece (+30) Greenland (+299) Grenada (+1) Guadeloupe (+590) Guam (+1) Guatemala (+502) Guernsey (+44) Guinea (+224) Guinea-Bissau (+245) Guyana (+592) Haiti (+509) Honduras (+504) Hong Kong (+852