    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/university-field-supervisor-traditional-pathway": {
      "title": "University Field Supervisor – Traditional Pathway -",
      "description": "University Field Supervisor – Traditional Pathway - University Field Supervisor – Traditional Pathway - Kiosk mode University Field Supervisor – Traditional Pathway 497377 Part-Time Reports To: Program Coordinator, College of Education Employment Type: Part-Time / Adjunct (as assigned per semester) Location: Partner District Campuses Description: The University Field Supervisor serves as a critical link between the UHCL’s educator preparation program and partner school districts. This role supports teacher resident candidates in applying coursework to classroom practice through observation, coaching, and feedback cycles. The supervisor ensures that candidates experience a cohesive, high-quality preparation aligned with state standards, district expectations, and the program’s residency model. Duties: Resident Supervision and Coaching Conduct a minimum of 4 formal observation cycle persemester using the university-approved rubric to include: Utilize the POP-Cycle to complete a pre- conference, observation, and post-conference with candidates to reinforce targeted instructional goals to provide timely, evidence-based feedback after each observation that promotesreflection and professional growth Complete a minimum of 3 walkthroughs per semester to provide ongoing feedback and coaching on the candidates’ progress Conduct a minimum of 6 seminar coaching/development sessions (90 to 120 minutes in length) to support candidates’ growth Support candidates in meeting program Performance Gates and demonstrating competencies outlined in the Teacher Residency Handbook Collaboration and Communication: Serve as a liaison between the university, district leadership, and cooperating teachers to ensure alignment of expectations and support structures Communicate regularly with CPDT director regarding candidate progress and needs Participate in calibration sessions, COE meetings, and professional learning to maintain inter-rater reliability and program consistency Documentation and Compliance: Complete observation forms, walkthrough forms, feedback notes, and candidate progress reports within program deadlines Document candidate attendance, professional dispositions, and compliance with university and district policies Maintain confidentiality and uphold professional standards as required by FERPA and university policy Program Support: Contribute to the continuous improvement of the Teacher Education Program by identifying trends and sharing field-based insights Support the preparation and mentoring of future teachers who embody the program’s mission of equity, excellence, and collaboration Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in Education or related field required; doctorate preferred Valid state teaching certificate and a minimum of three years of successful K–12 teaching experience Prior supervisory, instructional coaching, or teacher mentoring experience preferred Deep understanding of high-quality instruction, classroom management, and culturally responsive teaching Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills Reliable transportation to visit assigned campuses Work Expectations: Attend orientation and supervisor training sessions prior to and during the semester Conduct site visits and observations on a consistent schedule, maintaining visibility and accessibility to candidates and site staff Recommended postings Financial Coordinator (3 Vacancies) 497352 VP, Admin & Finance-Business Operations Full-Time Division of Administration and Finance University Field Supervisor – Traditional Pathway 497377 Academic Affairs-College of Edu Part-Time College of Education Lecturer, Computing Sciences 497317 Academic Affairs-College of S&E Full-Time College of Science and Engineering Lecturer, Computer Information Systems 497313 Academic Affairs-College of S&E Full-Time College of Science and Engineering Assistant Professor, Biology 497312 Academic Affairs-College of S&E Full-Time College of Science and Engineering Executive Director, Planning/Budget 497322 VP, Admin & Finance-Budget Office Full-Time Division of Administration & Finance Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Profile link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
