    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/lecturer-early-european-history-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Early European History",
      "description": "Lecturer, Early European History - Houston, Texas, United States Lecturer, Early European History - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Lecturer, Early European History 497374 Full-Time Liberal Arts Department : Humanities & Fine Arts Salary : Commensurate with Experience/Education Description : The History Program at the University of Houston-Clear Lake invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track position at the rank of Lecturer beginning Fall 2027. This position is not open for fully remote applicants. The position will be open until filled, with priority given to applications received by February 22, 2027. UHCL reserves the right to extend the search or not fill the position Duties: Teach four classes per semester (fall and spring) at the undergraduate and graduate levels. According to the needs of the History Program, courses may be in-person, hybrid, or online. Summer teaching is not required, although opportunities may be available Advise students as well as participating in committees and other university service. Qualifications Required: Earned doctoral degree in History with a demonstrated focus on ancient or medieval European history. Those with ABD status may apply, but the PhD must be earned before beginning the position at UHCL Experience teaching courses that cover early European history Willingness to teach existing or develop new courses in early European history according to the needs of the History Program and its students and to regularly teach an upper-level undergraduate survey of the ancient world Willingness to regularly teach the first half of the introductory-level World Civilization survey, covering the period from the ancient past until 1500 Demonstrated potential for effective teaching at UHCL including the use of innovative pedagogical strategies that will meet the needs of our students Preferred: An active research agenda in ancient or medieval European history and demonstrated potential to produce peer-reviewed scholarly publications Required Attachments by Candidate: 1) Curriculum Vitae containing the names, titles, and contact information for three professional references, 2) a Letter of Application that addresses the required and preferred qualifications, and highlights teaching experience and philosophy, 3) unofficial graduate transcripts, 4) scholarly writing sample of article or chapter length. Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be requested for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews, and a background check will be required. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Recommended postings Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor of Practice, Systems Engineering 497318 Academic Affairs-College of S&E Full-Time College of science and Engineering Assistant Professor, Biology 497312 Academic Affairs-College of S&E Full-Time College of Science and Engineering Lecturer, Early European History 497374 Academic Affairs-College of HSH Full-Time College of Human Sciences and Humanities Assistant Director of Strategic Communications and Welcome Center 497272 Strat Enrollment Mgmt-Admissions PH-LVL4 Full-Time Division of Strategic Enrollment Management Clinical Assistant Professor, Art Education 497372 Academic Affairs-College of HSH Full-Time College of Human Sciences and Humanities Assistant Professor, Art and Design 497373 Academic Affairs-College of HSH Full-Time College of Human Sciences and Humanities Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Profile link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
