    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/clinical-assistant-professor-art-education-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Art Education",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Art Education - Houston, Texas, United States Clinical Assistant Professor, Art Education - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Clinical Assistant Professor, Art Education 497372 Full-Time Humanities & Fine Arts Department : Humanities & Fine Arts Salary : Commensurate with Experience/Education Description : Founded in 1974, University of Houston-Clear Lake (UHCL) is a four-year institution, offering undergraduate, graduate and select doctoral degrees. UHCL is currently a bachelors and masters granting university with select doctoral programs. Located adjacent to the NASA-Johnson Space Center, the UHCL campus is set within the scenic Armand Bayou Nature Preserve, about 30 miles from both downtown Houston and Galveston Island. The Art and Design Program at the University of Houston-Clear Lake invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track position at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor in the area of Art Education. The Art and Design Program is housed within the College of Human Sciences and Humanities. This position would begin in August 2027. As Clinical Assistant Professor, the candidate will develop the Art Education/ EC-12 Certification concentration in the Art and Design BFA program. These responsibilities include teaching art education courses, serving as a liaison to the College of Education, working closely with the College of Education for student internship placement in local school districts, staying current with Texas Essential Knowledge and Skills (TEKS), developing and revising EC-12 Certification curriculum, mentoring BFA EC-12 Certification students in the development of their teaching and research portfolios, and working closely with the Art and Design faculty. Applications are accepted until the position is filled, and applications submitted on or before January 15, 2027, will receive full consideration. Duties: Teach four classes per semester (fall and spring). Summer teaching is not required, although opportunities may be available. Teaching courses: ARTS 2372 Integrating Visual Art in STEM ARTS 2379 Arts and the Child ARTS 4300 Methods in Elementary Art ARTS 4301 Methods in Secondary Art ARTS 4302 Crafts Design Develop/build curricula that meets the needs of the Art and Design Program and its students Advise students as well as participating in committees and other university service. Qualifications Required: Master of Arts in Art Education or equivalent area 3 years of experience in teaching at the college or university level Experience with mentoring/supervising student teachers Familiarity with the EC-12 certification process and Texas Essential Knowledge and Skills (TEKS) Preferred: Terminal degree in Art Education or equivalent area Texas teaching certification or the ability to acquire licensure Evidence of active research/artistic practice Complete applications will include the following: Completion of the online faculty application, including name, phone numbers, and email addresses for 3-5 professional references Letter of interest highlighting qualifications for position and evidence of teaching effectiveness. Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Evidence of teaching excellence Unofficial transcripts Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be requested for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews, and a background check will be required. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 31c6077b Last Name (required) 7095915a Email (required) 50444c5d Cell number 5c52f903 244 resu