    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-art-and-design-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Art and Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Art and Design - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant Professor, Art and Design - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Art and Design 497373 Full-Time Humanities & Fine Arts Department : Humanities & Fine Arts Salary : Commensurate with Experience/Education Description : Founded in 1974, UHCL is a four-year institution, offering undergraduate, graduate and select doctoral degrees. UHCL is currently a bachelors and masters granting university with select doctoral programs. Located adjacent to the NASA-Johnson Space Center, the UHCL campus is set within the scenic Armand Bayou Nature Preserve, about 30 miles from both downtown Houston and Galveston Island. The Art and Design Program at the University of Houston-Clear Lake (UHCL) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning August 2027. The Art and Design Program is housed within the College of Human Sciences and Humanities. Applications are accepted until the position is filled, and applications submitted on or before January 15, 2027, will receive full consideration. Duties: Teach three classes per semester (fall and spring). Summer teaching is not required, although opportunities may be available Lead and maintain the studio areas of painting/drawing Teach beginning, advanced and graduate level courses in painting/drawing Build curricula that meets the needs of the Art and Design Program and its students Maintain an active research practice with the potential for student involvement Advise students as well as participate in committees and other university service Qualifications Required: Master of Fine Arts in Painting or Drawing (or a related field) 3 years of experience in teaching at the college or university level Demonstrated ability to cover both traditional and contemporary techniques, and interdisciplinary practices in painting, drawing, and mixed media Exhibition record that shows an active, current research practice and demonstrated potential to produce research/artistic products sufficient for the award of tenure at UHCL Preferred: Ability to integrate digital components or technology into the areas of teaching and/or research Evidence of teaching excellence that aligns with the program’s emphasis on foundational skills in visual arts Complete applications will include the following: Completion of online faculty application, including current contact information for 3–5 professional references Letter of interest Curriculum vitae PDF portfolio with 20 images of current work and 20 images of recent student work (OR a link to an online portfolio provided in the CV) Statements of research and teaching interests Evidence of teaching excellence Unofficial transcripts Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be requested for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews, and a background check will be required. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 0c01e20c Last Name (required) 16c514b6 Email (required) 8d8d8e32 Cell number c4262f9a 244 results found No results found United States (+1) United Kingdom (+44) Australia (+61) Ireland (+353) Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Be