      "title": "Assistant Professor, Latin American History",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Latin American History - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant Professor, Latin American History - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Latin American History 497376 Full-Time Humanities & Fine Arts Department : Humanities & Fine Arts Salary : Commensurate with Experience/Education Description : The History Program at the University of Houston-Clear Lake invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning Fall 2027. This position is not open for fully remote applicants. The position will be open until filled, with priority given to applications received by January 18, 2026. UHCL reserves the right to extend the search or not fill the position. Duties: Teaching three classes per semester (fall and spring) at the undergraduate and graduate levels. According to the needs of the History Program, courses may be in-person, hybrid, or online. Summer teaching is not required, although opportunities may be available An active research agenda and producing peer-reviewed scholarly publications Advising students as well as participating in committees and other university service Qualifications Required: Earned doctoral degree in History with a demonstrated focus on Latin America. Those with ABD status may apply, but the PhD must be earned before beginning the position at UHCL Experience teaching courses that cover Latin American history Willingness to teach existing or develop new courses in Latin American history according to the needs of the History Program and its students Demonstrated potential for effective teaching at UHCL including the use of innovative pedagogical strategies that will meet the needs of our students An active research agenda in Latin American history and demonstrated potential to produce peer-reviewed scholarly publications sufficient for the award of tenure at UHCL Preferred: Demonstrated doctoral and current scholarly focus on the history of Mexico Required Attachments by Candidate: 1) Curriculum Vitae containing the names, titles, and contact information for three professional references, 2) a Letter of Application that addresses the required and preferred qualifications, and highlights teaching experience and philosophy, 3) unofficial graduate transcripts, 4) scholarly writing sample of article or chapter length. Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be requested for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews, and a background check will be required. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 3752b52d Last Name (required) cf5a0cae Email (required) 3c29be7e Cell number 825a298b 244 results found No results found United States (+1) United Kingdom (+44) Australia (+61) Ireland (+353) Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Ch