    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-or-professor-of-practice-systems-engineering-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor of Practice, Systems Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor of Practice, Systems Engineering - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor of Practice, Systems Engineering - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor of Practice, Systems Engineering 497318 Full-Time Engineering Department : Engineering Salary : Commensurate with Experience/Education Description : The Department of Engineering at the University of Houston–Clear Lake (UHCL) invites applications for a tenured or tenure-track Associate Professor, a tenure-track Assistant Professor, or a non-tenure-track Professor of Practice in the Systems Engineering M.S. program. The successful candidate will also serve as the Systems Engineering Program Director. This is a full-time faculty appointment with an anticipated start date of fall 2027. Candidates must demonstrate qualifications and accomplishments appropriate for the rank under consideration. Located near NASA’s Johnson Space Center and major engineering employers, UHCL offers opportunities for collaboration with industry and government. The Systems Engineering M.S. program, housed in the College of Science and Engineering, prepares graduates to design, analyze, integrate, and manage complex systems. The department also offers the following degree programs: Aerospace Engineering B.S., Computer Engineering B.S. and M.S., Mechanical Engineering B.S., Engineering Management M.S., and Software Engineering M.S. The Systems Engineering program’s interdisciplinary focus supports applications in aerospace, energy, healthcare, manufacturing, and other industries. The program also provides academic pathways for graduates of B.S. programs in Aerospace, Computer, and Mechanical Engineering to earn a master’s degree in Systems Engineering. For full consideration, submit application materials by January 15, 2027. Review of applications will begin as applications are received and continue until the position is filled. Anticipated start: August 2027. Duties: Faculty responsibilities: Teaching, research, and service Provide academic leadership and strategic direction for the Systems Engineering M.S. program Oversee course scheduling, curriculum coordination, and program assessment Support student recruitment, retention, advising, and degree completion Coordinate with faculty and administrators Director Responsibilites: Help strengthen industry and government partnerships Promote externally funded research and applied student projects Guide continuous improvement to address emerging systems engineering methods and workforce needs Qualifications Required: Earned doctorate in Systems Engineering or a related engineering discipline such as Industrial, Mechanical, or Aerospace Engineering Expertise in model-based systems engineering tools and their integration into the curriculum Evidence of ability to teach effectively at the graduate and undergraduate levels and strong potential for excellence in graduate instruction Evidence of effective student mentoring and advising Preferred: Industry or government experience, including partnerships in systems engineering or a related field Demonstrated ability to build partnerships with local industry A record of successful grant activity, funded research, or other externally supported projects Experience with the ABET accreditation process Demonstrated leadership and administrative experience at the department, program, or center level, including course scheduling, curriculum changes, and adjunct faculty recruitment and mentoring Evidence of a strong scholarly record in systems engineering Ability to teach in multiple course delivery modalities, including fully online and hybrid teaching Ability to design, develop, and implement fully online courses through the complete course development cycle Required Attachments by Candidate: Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Teaching Philosophy or Statement, Evidence of Effective Teaching , Unofficial Transcripts (official transcripts will be requested of all finalists). Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be requested for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews, and a background check will be required. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 1334ad98 Last Name (required) 3ef32ca2 Email (required) db0a8353 Cell number c640a70b 244 results found No results found United States (+1) United Kingdom (+44) Australia (+61) Ireland (+353) Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) Côte d’Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Curaçao (+599) Cyprus (+357) Czechia (+420) Denmark (+45) Djibouti (