      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Engineering Technology & Founding Program Director",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Engineering Technology & Founding Program Director - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant/Associate Professor, Engineering Technology & Founding Program Director - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate Professor, Engineering Technology & Founding Program Director 497315 Full-Time Engineering Department: Engineering Salary: Commensurate with Experience/Education Description: The Department of Engineering at the University of Houston–Clear Lake (UHCL) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor or Associate Professor to serve as the founding Program Director of its proposed Bachelor of Science in Engineering Technology. The anticipated start date is August 2027. The proposed 120-credit-hour program combines applied engineering sciences, materials, manufacturing, instrumentation, quality assurance, industrial operations, engineering management, occupational safety, and hands-on, project-based learning. Additional faculty appointments are anticipated as the program grows. Located in the Clear Lake area of Houston, near NASA Johnson Space Center and major aerospace, energy, petrochemical, and manufacturing employers, UHCL offers opportunities for industry engagement and applied education. The Engineering Department offers the following programs: Aerospace Engineering B.S., Computer Engineering B.S. and M.S., Mechanical Engineering B.S., Engineering Management M.S. and Software Engineering M.S. The program will draw on existing laboratories in mechanical, aerospace, occupational health and safety, and instructional facilities. The appointment is contingent upon final program approval by the Texas Higher Education Coordinating Board (THECB) and completion of applicable Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) approval requirements. For full consideration, submit application materials by January 15, 2027. Review of applications will begin as appropriate and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated appointment is for Fall 2027 and is contingent upon the external program approvals described above. Duties: Serve as the inaugural Engineering Technology Program Director, helping to shape the academic identity of the degree In collaboration with departmental faculty and university support units, lead the implementation and growth of the program Develop course schedules, coordinating course offerings and faculty teaching assignments, overseeing curriculum implementation and continuous improvement, supporting student recruitment/retention efforts, outreach activities, development of relationships with industry and community college partners Guide program assessment and preparations for accreditation through ABET’s Engineering Technology Accreditation Commission (ETAC) As a faculty member, teach undergraduate Engineering Technology courses, mentor students, develop industry-relevant learning experiences and capstone opportunities Establish and sustain an independent research program leading to peer-reviewed scholarly publications Pursue external research funding as appropriate Provide service to the Department, College, University, and profession. Qualifications Required: Earned Ph.D. in Engineering Technology, Mechanical Engineering, Industrial Engineering, or a closely related field Demonstrated experience teaching undergraduate Engineering Technology courses and an academic record appropriate for appointment at the Associate Professor rank Sufficient breadth in applied engineering to teach several courses in the proposed curriculum and to lead its development and administration, with preparation to contribute to teaching applied mechanics, materials, and/or manufacturing, with possible assignments including applied statics, applied dynamics, applied strength of materials, industrial materials with laboratory, and manufacturing technology with laboratory Demonstrated effective communication, collaborative leadership, a commitment to student success Ability to work with faculty and institutional partners across engineering, management, safety, and related areas Preferred: Administrative or leadership experience in Engineering Technology programs, such as program coordination, curriculum development, course scheduling, enrollment growth, faculty coordination, and assessment Experience with ABET ETAC criteria or accreditation preparation Industry partnerships, applied scholarship, community college transfer pathways, and laboratory- or project-based instruction will be viewed favorably Teaching breadth in electrical systems, instrumentation, technical project supervision, and other applied Engineering Technology areas is desirable; additional teaching opportunities may include the Instrumentation Laboratory for Engineering Technology, and the Engineering Technology capstone sequence, depending on qualifications and program needs Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be requested for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews, and a background check will be required. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) cadd26c8 Last Name (required) 1d17a4bd Email (required) 1d7d502a Cell number 37a6abac 244 results found No results found United States (+1) United Kingdom (+44) Australia (+61) Ireland (+353) Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Aust