    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/university-field-supervisor-teacher-residency-program": {
      "title": "University Field Supervisor – Teacher Residency Program -",
      "description": "University Field Supervisor – Teacher Residency Program - University Field Supervisor – Teacher Residency Program - Kiosk mode University Field Supervisor – Teacher Residency Program 497380 Part-Time Description: The University Field Supervisor serves as a critical link between the UHCL’s educator preparation program and partner school districts. This role supports teacher resident candidates in applying coursework to classroom practice through observation, coaching, and feedback cycles. The supervisor ensures that residents experience a cohesive, high-quality preparation aligned with state standards, district expectations, and the program’s residency model. Duties: Resident Supervision and Coaching Conduct a minimum of 2 formal observation cycles per semester using the university-approved rubric to include: Pre- and post-conferences with residents to reinforce targeted instructional goals Timely, evidence-based feedback after each observation that promotes reflection and professional growth Complete a minimum of 4 walkthroughs per semester to provide ongoing feedback and coaching on the residents’ growth Support residents in meeting program performance gates and demonstrating competencies outlined in the Teacher Residency Handbook Collaboration and Communication Serve as a liaison between the university, district site coordinators, and host teachers to ensure alignment of expectations and support structures Communicate regularly with university faculty and residency program leads regarding candidate progress and needs Participate monthly in calibration sessions with the district Site Coordinator and professional learning as needed to maintain inter-rater reliability and program consistency Documentation and Compliance Complete observation forms, feedback notes, and candidate progress reports within program deadlines Document resident attendance, professional dispositions, and compliance with university and district policies Maintain confidentiality and uphold professional standards as required by FERPA and university policy Program Support Contribute to the continuous improvement of the residency program by identifying trends and sharing field-based insights Support the preparation and mentoring of future teachers who embody the program’s mission of equity, excellence, and collaboration Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in Education or related field required; doctorate preferred Valid state teaching certificate and a minimum of three years of successful PK–12 teaching experience Prior supervisory, instructional coaching, or teacher mentoring experience preferred Deep understanding of high-quality instruction, classroom management, and culturally responsive teaching Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills Reliable transportation to visit assigned campuses Work Expectations: Attend orientation and supervisor training sessions prior to and during the semester Conduct site visits and observations on a consistent schedule, maintaining visibility and accessibility to residents and site staff Participate in virtual or in-person calibration and professional development meetings (approx. 1 hour per month) Apply now First Name (required) a61e79d8 Last Name (required) 3e2b1fca Email (required) e2cf43d4 Cell number eb2fda74 244 results found No results found United States (+1) United Kingdom (+44) Australia (+61) Ireland (+353) Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Bur