    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-mechanical-engineering-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Mechanical Engineering - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant Professor, Mechanical Engineering - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Mechanical Engineering 497314 Full-Time Engineering Department : Engineering Salary : Commensurate with Experience/Education Description : The Mechanical Engineering (MENG) Program at the University of Houston–Clear Lake (UHCL) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate engineering education, develop an independent research program leading to peer-reviewed publications and pursuit of external funding, mentor students, and provide service to the program, university, and profession, including support for ABET accreditation activities. UHCL’s ABET-accredited B.S. in Mechanical Engineering combines hands-on engineering education with opportunities for undergraduate research in the Houston – Clear Lake region, near NASA Johnson Space Center and a substantial community of aerospace, energy, chemical, and manufacturing employers. The program has experienced significant growth in recent years. The department offers the following programs: Aerospace Engineering B.S., Computer Engineering B.S. and M.S., Mechanical Engineering B.S., Engineering Management M.S. and Software Engineering M.S. The department’s graduate programs offer pathways for mechanical engineering graduates to earn master’s degrees while providing opportunities for mechanical engineering faculty to mentor graduate students. For full consideration, submit application materials by January 15, 2027. Review of applications will begin as applications are received and continue until the position is filled. Anticipated start: August 2027. Duties: Establish a sustainable scholarly agenda, seek external support as appropriate, and engage undergraduates in meaningful research and design experiences. UHCL’s teaching and research environment includes thermal-fluid, materials-testing, composites, additive-manufacturing, and computational resource Qualifications Required: Earned Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline is required by the start of the appointment Demonstrated expertise in thermal-fluid sciences and the ability to teach Thermodynamics, Fluid Mechanics, and Heat Transfer, displayed through evidence of doctoral research, scholarly work, or substantial relevant engineering experience Demonstrated strong commitment to effective undergraduate teaching, student mentoring, and clear written and oral communication Preferred: Teaching experience Ability to teach a broad set of thermal-fluid courses, including Thermal/Fluid System Design, Thermal/Fluid Laboratory, or advanced computational thermal-fluid electives Ability to teach Dynamics and Control of Mechanical Systems or other mechanical engineering courses Familiarity with ABET accreditation processes and continuous improvement Practical experience in industry or government Professional licensure Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be requested for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews, and a background check will be required. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) cc6ca578 Last Name (required) 024bf65d Email (required) 8a89e374 Cell number d6d97304 244 results found No results found United States (+1) United Kingdom (+44) Australia (+61) Ireland (+353) Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) Ameri