    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/instructional-assistant-professor-lecturer-mechanical-engineering-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant Professor/Lecturer, Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Instructional Assistant Professor/Lecturer, Mechanical Engineering - Houston, Texas, United States Instructional Assistant Professor/Lecturer, Mechanical Engineering - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Instructional Assistant Professor/Lecturer, Mechanical Engineering 497316 Full-Time Engineering Department: Engineering Salary: Commensurate with Experience/Education Description: The Mechanical Engineering (MENG) Program at the University of Houston–Clear Lake (UHCL) invites applications for a teaching-focused faculty position at the rank of Instructional Assistant Professor or Lecturer beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will teach foundational engineering courses and contribute directly to student success in the early engineering curriculum. UHCL’s ABET-accredited B.S. in Mechanical Engineering emphasizes laboratory and project-based learning in a region with extensive aerospace, energy, chemical, and manufacturing activity. The program has experienced significant growth in recent years. This position offers an opportunity to help students build the technical foundation, confidence, and academic habits needed to progress through that growing program. The department offers the following programs: Aerospace Engineering B.S., Computer Engineering B.S. and M.S., Mechanical Engineering B.S., Engineering Management M.S. and Software Engineering M.S.. The role is teaching-focused; an independently funded research program is not required. For full consideration, submit application materials by January 15, 2027. Review of applications will begin as applications are received and continue until the position is filled. Anticipated start: August 2027 Duties: Hands-on engineering instruction, coordinating course and laboratory activities as appropriate Participation in assessment and ABET-related continuous improvement Provision of appropriate departmental service Devotion to student success in early engineering courses, including identifying students who are struggling academically, coordinating appropriate academic support and referrals, and helping students establish and follow actionable plans to regain satisfactory progress; to be coordinated with faculty, advising, and university student-support services Qualifications Required: An earned Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Engineering Education (with M.S. in Mechanical Engineering) or a closely related engineering discipline is required for appointment as Instructional Assistant Professor An earned master’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline is required for appointment as Lecturer, with applicants able to teach Engineering Graphics using SolidWorks™, Statics, Dynamics, and Introduction to Engineering Demonstrated strong commitment to effective undergraduate teaching, student mentoring, and clear written and oral communication Preferred: Preference will be given to candidates with teaching experience Demonstrated experience supporting students in gateway STEM courses through academic interventions, tutoring, mentoring, or supplemental instruction Ability to teach Dynamics and Control, Finite Element Analysis, Mechatronics, Robotics, or other engineering courses Familiarity with ABET accreditation processes and continuous improvement Demonstrated relevant industrial experience Hold professional registration Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be requested for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews, and a background check will be required. This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 46414441 Last Name (required) 904b36a1 Email (required) adbe3fe8 Cell number 23c6803e 244 results found No results found United States (+1) United Kingdom (+44) Australia (+61) Ireland (+353) Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) Côte d’Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Curaçao (+599) Cyprus (+357) Czechia (+420) Denmark (+45) Djibouti (+253) Dominica (+1) Dominican Republic (+1) Ecuador (+593) Egypt (+20) El Salvador (+503) Equatorial Guinea (+240) Eritrea (+291) Estonia (+372) Eswatini (+268) Ethiopia (+251) Falkland Islands (Islas Malvinas) (+500) Faroe Islands (+298) Fiji (+679) Finland (+358) France (+33) French Guiana (+594) French Polynesia (+689) Gabon (+241) Gambia (+220) Georgia (+995) Germany (+49) Ghana (+233) Gibraltar (+350) Greece (+30) Greenland (+299) Grenada (+1) Guadeloupe (+590) Guam (+1) Guatemala (+502) Guernsey (+44) Guinea (+224) Guinea-Bissau (+245) Guyana (+592) Haiti (+509) Honduras (+504) Hong Kong (+852) Hungary (+36) Iceland (+354) India (+91) Indonesia (+62) Iran (+98) Iraq (+964) Isle of Man (+44) Israel (